Decision: retain the single 8 MiB application Tokio runtime and retry transient macOS watchdog identity inspections instead of treating them as process death.
Reason: after the regex-only fix, a second real UI SIGBUS occurred in inspect_extensions on a 2 MiB worker, proving the stack depth belongs to the shared Agent future. A temporary inspection failure does not prove that the parent or protected shell has exited.
Validation: cargo test macos_parent_guard --lib (5 passed); cargo test --test shell_parent_death_macos -- --nocapture (2 passed, 0 failed, 1 ignored); cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings (exit 0); cargo test (5657 passed, 0 failed, 22 ignored).
